---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Succession & Probate" description="Succession planning, letters of administration and probate in Cameroon, including estates with heirs abroad.">
<div>
  <section style="max-width:1360px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(48px,7vw,104px) clamp(20px,5vw,80px) clamp(36px,4vw,56px)">
    <a href="/practices/" class="lnk" style="background:none;border:0;padding:0;cursor:pointer;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#007EA7;margin-bottom:26px">← Practices</a>
    <h1 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(36px,5.2vw,68px);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;max-width:22ch">Succession &amp; Probate</h1>
    <p style="font-size:clamp(17px,1.4vw,20px);line-height:1.7;color:#38484f;max-width:66ch;margin:32px 0 0">We help families plan for succession and settle estates, including estates that include land and heirs living outside Cameroon.</p>
  </section>
  <hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14);margin:0" />
  <section style="max-width:1360px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(40px,5vw,72px) clamp(20px,5vw,80px) clamp(56px,7vw,96px)">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px">
      <div style="grid-column:4 / span 7;min-width:280px">
        <section data-reveal="1" style="padding:0 0 40px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(24px,2.3vw,30px);margin:0 0 18px">Succession planning</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 0px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Wills, the appointment of executors and guardians, and planning for family property and family businesses. Customary succession still governs many estates in practice and does not always produce the statutory result, particularly for spouses and children. We plan so that the question is settled in advance rather than argued after death.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-reveal="1" style="padding:40px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(24px,2.3vw,30px);margin:0 0 18px">Letters of administration</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 0px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Where there is no will, we apply for letters of administration, identify the persons entitled to administer and inherit, collect and value the estate, and deal with land certificates and bank accounts held in the deceased’s name.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-reveal="1" style="padding:40px 0 0;">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(24px,2.3vw,30px);margin:0 0 18px">Probate matters</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 16px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Applications for probate of a will, advice to executors on their duties, distribution to beneficiaries, and contested applications between family members. For heirs abroad we arrange local representation and coordinate with foreign proceedings.</p><p style="font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7b82;margin:0;max-width:68ch">General information about the firm’s practice, not legal advice.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>
